arXiv:2510.04384v1 [cs.AI] 05 Oct 2025</div>
</div><div class="ltx_page_content">
<article class="ltx_document ltx_authors_1line">
<h1 class="ltx_title ltx_title_document">LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search</h1>
<div class="ltx_authors">
<span class="ltx_creator ltx_role_author">
<span class="ltx_personname">Adam Ballew   Jingbo Wang   Shaogang Ren
</span><span class="ltx_author_notes"><span class="ltx_author_notes_content">
<span class="ltx_contact ltx_role_affiliation"><span class="ltx_contact_name">Affiliation: </span>Department of Computer Science and Engineering
<br class="ltx_break">University of Tennessee at Chattanooga
<br class="ltx_break">615 McCallie Ave, Chattanooga, TN 37403 
<br class="ltx_break">Email: adam.ballew94@gmail.com  ydk297@mocs.utc.edu  shaogang-ren@utc.edu
</span></span></span></span></div>

<div id="abstract1" class="ltx_abstract"><h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_abstract">Abstract</h6>
    
<p id="abstract1.1" class="ltx_p">Bayesian Optimization (BO) has been widely used to efficiently optimize expensive black-box functions with limited evaluations. In this paper, we investigate the use of BO for prompt engineering to enhance text classification with Large Language Models (LLMs). We employ an LLM-powered Gaussian Process (GP) as the surrogate model to estimate the performance of different prompt candidates. These candidates are generated by an LLM through the expansion of a set of seed prompts and are subsequently evaluated using an Upper Confidence Bound (UCB) acquisition function in conjunction with the GP posterior. The optimization process iteratively refines the prompts based on a subset of the data, aiming to improve classification accuracy while reducing the number of API calls by leveraging the prediction uncertainty of the LLM-based GP. The proposed BO-LLM<span id="footnote1" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">1</sup>
          <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">1</span>
          
          
        <span class="ltx_ref ltx_nolink ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter ltx_ref_self">https://github.com/ShaogangRen/BO-LLM</span></span></span></span>
algorithm is evaluated on two datasets, and its advantages are discussed in detail in this paper.</p>
  
</div>
<div class="ltx_keywords">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_title_keywords">Index Terms: </h6>Bayesian Optimization, Prompt Engineering, LLM, Gaussian Process, Upper Confidence Bound

</div>
<section id="S1" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">I </span><span id="S1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Introduction</span></h2>

<div id="S1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The advancements in Large Language Models (LLMs), such as OpenAI’s GPT, have allowed their application in various Natural Language Processing (NLP) tasks, including text classification <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">1</a>]</cite>, question answering <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">2</a>]</cite>, and text generation <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib3" title="" class="ltx_ref">3</a>]</cite>.
However, the performance of these models is highly sensitive to the structure and wording of the prompt it is given, making prompt optimization an important problem to solve <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">To address this, we propose using Bayesian Optimization (BO), a powerful framework for derivative-free optimization of expensive black-box functions <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, to systematically refine prompts for binary classification tasks. BO has been successfully applied to hyperparameter tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>]</cite>, neural architecture search <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib7" title="" class="ltx_ref">7</a>]</cite>, and model calibration <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">8</a>, <a href="#bib.bib9" title="" class="ltx_ref">9</a>]</cite>, demonstrating its effectiveness in high-dimensional discrete optimization problems. The key challenge lies in optimizing the prompt structure to maximize classification accuracy while minimizing the number of expensive API calls. BO offers an efficient strategy by modeling the relationship between different prompts and their classification performance using a Gaussian Process (GP) as a surrogate function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>.
The optimization process is guided by an Upper Confidence Bound (UCB)
acquisition function <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>, which balances exploration (testing new prompts with high uncertainty) and exploitation (selecting prompts with a high estimated accuracy) to iteratively select prompt candidates.
Our BO-LLM framework combines this GP surrogate and UCB acquisition with an LLM-based expansion mechanism to generate candidates.</p>
</div>
<div id="S1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Our contributions are: (i) introducing BO-LLM as a black-box prompt
optimization framework, (ii) evaluating it on LIAR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> and ETHOS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite> against ProTeGi <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>,
and (iii) showing adaptability to multi-turn QA.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">II </span><span id="S2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Background</span></h2>

<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">II-A</span> </span><span id="S2.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prompt Engineering and LLM Performance</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The quality of a prompt is crucial to LLM performance in fulfilling a user’s request, with key aspects being its clarity, relevancy, and structure. The specific wording has been shown to greatly affect the quality of the response, and a prompt that clearly states the user’s request with minimal irrelevant information generally yields better outcomes <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">15</a>, <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">4</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Prompt engineering is the practice of refining a prompt until the LLM’s output is as close to the desired outcome as possible. Historically, this has been a time-consuming process requiring human-driven trial-and-error, where the user’s domain knowledge significantly determines the quality of the final prompt. An automated prompt engineering process can help to alleviate these problems by reducing or completely removing this manual loop and leveraging the LLM’s vast knowledge to generate effective prompts.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">LLMs interact with users through a prompt–response paradigm, where the prompt’s formulation strongly influences the output’s usefulness. For example, prompts that clearly state the request first before providing relevant context are consistently more effective. Given that manual prompt crafting is both time-consuming and dependent on user expertise, automated methods are desirable to improve efficiency and reproducibility. This motivates the use of systematic frameworks, such as BO, to automate the exploration of the prompt space.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">II-B</span> </span><span id="S2.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Bayesian Optimization</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">BO is a sequential model-based optimization framework well-suited for optimizing black-box functions that are expensive to evaluate. As outlined by Brochu et al. <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>, instead of directly optimizing the objective function, BO constructs a surrogate model—commonly a GP <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">10</a>]</cite>—that approximates the objective based on prior observations. This probabilistic model provides not only an estimation of the function’s value but also its uncertainty across the input space. The core steps are as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 1: Initialization.</span> A surrogate model, such as a GP, is chosen. The GP is defined by a mean function <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and a kernel (or covariance function) <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x,x^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x,x^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>, which computes the relationship between observation data point.</p>
<table id="S2.E1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(x)\sim\mathcal{GP}(\mu(x),k(x,x^{\prime}))" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(x)\sim\mathcal{GP}(\mu(x),k(x,x^{\prime}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(1)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">An initial observation dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math> is collected, where <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> represents an input (a feature vector or a prompt) and <math id="S2.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> is its corresponding evaluation from the objective function (accuracy).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 2: Posterior Inference.</span> Given the current dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> (the prior), the GP is fitted to obtain a posterior distribution over the objective function. This posterior captures our updated belief about the function after observing the data.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 3: Acquisition Function.</span>
We adopt the Upper Confidence Bound acquisition, which balances exploration and exploitation.
See Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Acquisition Function ‣ III-A Bayesian Optimization Formulation ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>) in Sec. III-F for the exact form used in our framework.
UCB also enjoys theoretical guarantees in the bandit setting <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p5" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 4: Sample Point Selection.</span>
Choose the next point by maximizing the acquisition:</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{\text{next}}=\arg\max_{x}\alpha(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mtext>next</mtext></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>x</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{\text{next}}=\arg\max_{x}\alpha(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.p5.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.p5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> is the UCB acquisition defined in Eq. (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In Acquisition Function ‣ III-A Bayesian Optimization Formulation ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p6" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS2.p6.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.p6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Step 5: Objective Evaluation and Update.</span> The true objective function is evaluated at <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{next}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{next}</annotation></semantics></math> to get a new observation <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{next}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{next}</annotation></semantics></math>. This new data point <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x_{next},y_{next})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x_{next},y_{next})</annotation></semantics></math> is added to the dataset <math id="S2.SS2.p6.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, and the process repeats from Step 2<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>. This loop continues until a termination condition, such as a fixed number of iterations, is met.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S2.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">II-C</span> </span><span id="S2.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Related Work</span></h3>

<div id="S2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Beyond manual crafting, several automated prompt optimization techniques have emerged.
One prominent approach is Automatic Prompt Engineer (APE) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib16" title="" class="ltx_ref">16</a>]</cite>, which
leverages an LLM to generate a diverse set of instruction candidates and then selects the best one based on a chosen scoring function. This paradigm has been further explored
in Optimization by PROmpting (OPRO) <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">17</a>]</cite>, where the LLM iteratively generates improved prompts based on past performance feedback. Unlike our model-based approach, these methods rely on a generate-and-test loop without an explicit surrogate model capturing prompt-performance relationships.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Another line of work frames prompt optimization as a discrete search problem.
RLPrompt <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">18</a>]</cite> trains a policy network using reinforcement learning to generate prompts that maximize task accuracy. Prompt tuning methods such as prefix-tuning <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">19</a>]</cite> and soft prompts <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib20" title="" class="ltx_ref">20</a>]</cite> optimize continuous embeddings rather than discrete text, but require access to model parameters.
In contrast, our Bayesian approach treats the LLM as a black box and leverages a GP surrogate for sample-efficient exploration of the discrete prompt space.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS3.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S2.SS3.p3.1" class="ltx_p">ProTeGi is an algorithm that uses gradient-inspired edits and beam search to automatically optimize prompts. It generates candidate prompts from a seed by identifying errors on a small dataset, prompting an LLM to generate “gradients” (i.e., critiques), and then using another LLM to apply these critiques to edit the prompt. It performed well on several binary classification tasks, including LIAR and ETHOS, which we use as a baseline. BO-LLM uses components from ProTeGi, particularly its expansion function, but replaces the heuristic search with a formal BO framework<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">III </span><span id="S3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Methodology</span></h2>

<div id="S3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We propose BO-LLM, a framework that applies BO to prompt search. The objective is to identify prompts that maximize classification accuracy. Unlike heuristic methods, BO-LLM explicitly models the performance landscape of candidate prompts with a GP surrogate, enabling sample-efficient optimization. Figure <a href="#S3.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a> illustrates how prompts are transformed from text to numerical representations for optimization.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04384v1/num_representation.png" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/349;" width="476" height="349" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 1: </span>How prompts are transformed from textual information to numerical information.</figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="S3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">As illustrated in Fig. <a href="#S3.F1" title="Fig. 1 ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>, each textual prompt <math id="S3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is turned into a numerical object in three complementary ways:
(i) the prediction vector <math id="S3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math> on the fixed control minibatch <math id="S3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math>,
(ii) the surrogate’s posterior mean <math id="S3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(p)</annotation></semantics></math> and uncertainty <math id="S3.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(p)</annotation></semantics></math> computed from <math id="S3.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, and
(iii) the acquisition score <math id="S3.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha(p)</annotation></semantics></math> derived from <math id="S3.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(\mu,\sigma)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(\mu,\sigma)</annotation></semantics></math>.
These representations jointly support sample-efficient selection during BO-LLM.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">III-A</span> </span><span id="S3.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Bayesian Optimization Formulation</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math> denote the discrete prompt space. Given a labeled
dataset <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x_{i},y_{i})\}_{i=1}^{N}</annotation></semantics></math>, our objective is to
maximize the test accuracy of an LLM queried with prompt <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in\mathcal{P}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒫</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in\mathcal{P}</annotation></semantics></math>:</p>
<table id="S3.E2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E2.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f(p)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\big[\mathbbm{1}\{\mathrm{LLM}_{p}(x)=y\}\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>LLM</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(p)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,y)\sim\mathcal{D}}\big[\mathbbm{1}\{\mathrm{LLM}_{p}(x)=y\}\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(2)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each evaluation on a subset of <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, i.e., <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, yields a noisy observation
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(p)=f(p)+\varepsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(p)=f(p)+\varepsilon</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon\sim\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2})</annotation></semantics></math>. We maintain a cache of observations
<math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D=\{(p_{i},a(p_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>a</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{(p_{i},a(p_{i})\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Representation</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To build the surrogate model, each prompt <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> is mapped to a
prediction vector <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{p}\in\{0,1\}^{|B_{GP}|}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{p}\in\{0,1\}^{|B_{GP}|}</annotation></semantics></math> on a fixed
control minibatch <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">5</a>]</cite>.
This vector serves as the prompt’s numerical representation. The
similarity between two prompts <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{j}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{j}</annotation></semantics></math> is measured via a
Radial Basis Function (RBF) kernel:</p>
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(p_{i},p_{j})=\exp\left(-\frac{\|\hat{y}_{p_{i}}-\hat{y}_{p_{j}}\|_{2}^{2}}{2R}\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></msub><mo>−</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(p_{i},p_{j})=\exp\left(-\frac{\|\hat{y}_{p_{i}}-\hat{y}_{p_{j}}\|_{2}^{2}}{2R}\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(3)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">which captures the intuition that prompts with similar prediction
patterns on <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> have correlated accuracies. The kernel
hyperparameter <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> was set empirically to 1.0 after preliminary runs
indicated stable performance at this value.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The mean of each prompt candidate’s prediction accuracy regarding <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> is calculated as follows:</p>
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="~m(p)=\frac{1}{|B_{GP}|}\sum_{i\in B_{GP}}\mathbbm{1}\{\hat{y}_{i}=y_{i}\}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></munder><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">~m(p)=\frac{1}{|B_{GP}|}\sum_{i\in B_{GP}}\mathbbm{1}\{\hat{y}_{i}=y_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(4)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the predicted value for a given sentence and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> represents the ground truth label.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Surrogate Model</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Given observations <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D=\{(p_{i},a(p_{i}))\}_{i=1}^{n}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>D</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>n</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D=\{(p_{i},a(p_{i}))\}_{i=1}^{n}</annotation></semantics></math>, we update the GP
prior over <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> using Bayes’ rule:</p>
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(f\,|\,D)\ \propto\ P(D\,|\,f)\,P(f)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>D</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em">∝</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(f\,|\,D)\ \propto\ P(D\,|\,f)\,P(f).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(5)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Here <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(f)</annotation></semantics></math> is the GP prior over functions and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="P(D\,|\,f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>P</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0.170em">|</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">P(D\,|\,f)</annotation></semantics></math> is the
Gaussian likelihood with observation noise. Conditioning the joint
Gaussian yields the closed-form posterior used in our surrogate
(see Appendix <a href="#A0.SS5" title="-E Hyperparameters and Sketch of GP Posterior Derivation ‣ VI Discussion and Conclusion ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">-E</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We can further calculate the posterior mean for each prompt using:</p>
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(p)=m(p)+\mathbf{k}_{p}^{\top}(\mathbf{K}+\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{m})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>𝐦</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(p)=m(p)+\mathbf{k}_{p}^{\top}(\mathbf{K}+\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbf{I})^{-1}(\mathbf{a}-\mathbf{m})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(6)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{k}_{p}=[k(p,p_{1}),\ldots,k(p,p_{n})]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{k}_{p}=[k(p,p_{1}),\ldots,k(p,p_{n})]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the
covariance vector between the new prompt <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> and all observed prompts
in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{K}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>𝐊</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{K}</annotation></semantics></math> is the <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n\times n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n\times n</annotation></semantics></math> kernel matrix with entries
<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K_{ij}=k(p_{i},p_{j})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K_{ij}=k(p_{i},p_{j})</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{a}=[a(p_{1}),\ldots,a(p_{n})]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{a}=[a(p_{1}),\ldots,a(p_{n})]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>
is the vector of observed accuracies of the prompts in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> on set <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{m}=[m(p_{1}),\ldots,m(p_{n})]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>𝐦</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>n</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{m}=[m(p_{1}),\ldots,m(p_{n})]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math> is the vector of prediction accuracy of the prompts in <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> on set <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> as given in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In Data Representation ‣ III-A Bayesian Optimization Formulation ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.1" class="ltx_p">Given the observation history <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, the GP posterior provides a
predictive distribution for any new prompt. The posterior mean
<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(p)</annotation></semantics></math> and variance <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(p)</annotation></semantics></math> are calculated as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma^{2}(p)=k(p,p)-\mathbf{k}_{p}^{\top}(\mathbf{K}+\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbf{I})^{-1}\mathbf{k}_{p}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>𝐊</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>σ</mi><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐈</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>𝐤</mi><mi>p</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma^{2}(p)=k(p,p)-\mathbf{k}_{p}^{\top}(\mathbf{K}+\sigma_{\varepsilon}^{2}\mathbf{I})^{-1}\mathbf{k}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Acquisition Function</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">After generating a set of new candidates, we use the GP posterior to
estimate their mean accuracy <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(p)</annotation></semantics></math> and uncertainty <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma(p)</annotation></semantics></math>.
The Upper Confidence Bound acquisition function is the key
component for balancing exploration and exploitation:</p>
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha_{\text{UCB}}(p)=\mu(p)+\kappa\sigma(p)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>α</mi><mtext>UCB</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha_{\text{UCB}}(p)=\mu(p)+\kappa\sigma(p)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> controls the exploration-exploitation trade-off.
The first term <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(p)</annotation></semantics></math> encourages <em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exploitation</em> by favoring
prompts with high predicted accuracy, while the second term
<math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa\sigma(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa\sigma(p)</annotation></semantics></math> encourages <em id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.2.2" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">exploration</em> by favoring prompts
with high uncertainty. We select the prompt <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> that maximizes this
score, evaluate its true accuracy on <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and add the result
to our observation data for the next round. UCB enjoys theoretical
guarantees in the bandit setting and is particularly robust under
evaluation noise <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib11" title="" class="ltx_ref">11</a>]</cite>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In our implementation, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is annealed linearly from 2.0 to 0.5
over the 10 optimization rounds, transitioning from exploration-heavy
behavior in early rounds to exploitation-focused selection as the
surrogate model becomes more confident.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Alternative Acquisition (EI)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Besides UCB, Expected Improvement (EI) is a standard choice <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">6</a>, <a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">21</a>]</cite>:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{EI}(p)=\big(\mu(p)-f^{\star}-\xi\big)\Phi(Z)+\sigma(p)\phi(Z),\quad Z=\frac{\mu(p)-f^{\star}-\xi}{\sigma(p)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>EI</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mi>Z</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>ξ</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{EI}(p)=\big(\mu(p)-f^{\star}-\xi\big)\Phi(Z)+\sigma(p)\phi(Z),\quad Z=\frac{\mu(p)-f^{\star}-\xi}{\sigma(p)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\star}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>f</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\star}</annotation></semantics></math> is the best observed accuracy, <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Phi/\phi" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Φ</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>ϕ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Phi/\phi</annotation></semantics></math> are the
standard normal CDF/PDF, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\xi\!\geq\!0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ξ</mi><mo lspace="0.108em">≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\xi\!\geq\!0</annotation></semantics></math> controls exploration. We
report UCB results for its robustness under evaluation noise, but EI
is drop-in compatible with our pipeline.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Surrogate Details and Model Parameter Learning</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We optimize kernel parameters <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(R,\sigma^{2})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(R,\sigma^{2})</annotation></semantics></math> by maximizing the log marginal likelihood:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p(\mathbf{a}|\theta)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}^{\top}K_{\theta}^{-1}\mathbf{a}-\tfrac{1}{2}\log|K_{\theta}|-\tfrac{n}{2}\log 2\pi." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>𝐚</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐚</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo fence="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mi>n</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>π</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p(\mathbf{a}|\theta)=-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}^{\top}K_{\theta}^{-1}\mathbf{a}-\tfrac{1}{2}\log|K_{\theta}|-\tfrac{n}{2}\log 2\pi.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Gradient:</p>
<table id="S3.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\partial\log p}{\partial\theta}=\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}^{\top}K_{\theta}^{-1}\tfrac{\partial K_{\theta}}{\partial\theta}K_{\theta}^{-1}\mathbf{a}-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}\!\left(K_{\theta}^{-1}\tfrac{\partial K_{\theta}}{\partial\theta}\right)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>𝐚</mi><mo>⊤</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>𝐚</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mpadded style="width:0.670em;" width="0.670em"><mi>tr</mi></mpadded><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><msub><mi>K</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial\log p}{\partial\theta}=\tfrac{1}{2}\mathbf{a}^{\top}K_{\theta}^{-1}\tfrac{\partial K_{\theta}}{\partial\theta}K_{\theta}^{-1}\mathbf{a}-\tfrac{1}{2}\mathrm{tr}\!\left(K_{\theta}^{-1}\tfrac{\partial K_{\theta}}{\partial\theta}\right).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.3" class="ltx_p">A full derivation is in Appendix <a href="#A0.SS5" title="-E Hyperparameters and Sketch of GP Posterior Derivation ‣ VI Discussion and Conclusion ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">-E</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S3.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">III-B</span> </span><span id="S3.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Overall Algorithm</span></h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The optimization loop of BO-LLM proceeds in rounds.
At each round the surrogate GP is updated, new candidates
are generated from current seeds, and the most promising
candidate is selected via the acquisition function. The
selected prompt is then evaluated and added to the cache.
This process is summarized in Algorithm <a href="#alg1" title="Algorithm 1 ‣ III-B Overall Algorithm ‣ III Methodology ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg1" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 1</span> </span> BO-LLM: Overall Loop</figcaption>
<div id="alg1.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg1.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            Seeds <math id="alg1.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, control batch <math id="alg1.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, evaluation batch <math id="alg1.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>, rounds <math id="alg1.l1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg1.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="alg1.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg1.l2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
              Fit GP on cache <math id="alg1.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{Expand}(S_{t-1},B_{\alpha})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>Expand</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}\leftarrow\mathrm{Expand}(S_{t-1},B_{\alpha})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg1.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}\leftarrow\arg\max_{p\in C_{t}}\mu_{t}(p)+\kappa_{t}\sigma_{t}(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>κ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}\leftarrow\arg\max_{p\in C_{t}}\mu_{t}(p)+\kappa_{t}\sigma_{t}(p)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              Evaluate <math id="alg1.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="a(p_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">a(p_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg1.l6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, update <math id="alg1.l6.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              Update seeds <math id="alg1.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg1.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg1.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg1.l8.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg1.l8.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
</div>
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The overall optimization loop is summarized in Algorithm 1. The process is iterative, where in each round <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> (from 1 to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>T</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T</annotation></semantics></math>), we update our model based on the accumulated data. We maintain a cache, denoted as <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, which stores all prompt-accuracy pairs evaluated so far. At the beginning of round <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>, we use the cache from the previous round, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t-1}</annotation></semantics></math>, to fit the GP surrogate model. A new prompt <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> is then selected and evaluated, and the cache is updated to <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> by adding the new observation <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(p_{t},a(p_{t}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(p_{t},a(p_{t}))</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">IV </span><span id="S4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Implementation of BO-LLM</span></h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we discuss the implementation of the BO-LLM algorithm.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">IV-A</span> </span><span id="S4.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">System Architecture</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F2" title="Fig. 2 ‣ IV-A System Architecture ‣ IV Implementation of BO-LLM ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a> presents the complete architecture of BO-LLM, illustrating the interaction between key components: the dataset <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math>, the two evaluation minibatches (<math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>), the LLM-based expansion function,
the GP surrogate, and the UCB acquisition mechanism. The bidirectional arrows indicate the iterative refinement process where selected prompts <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> are evaluated on the objective function, and their observations are fed back to update the surrogate model.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F2" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.04384v1/original_flowchart.png" id="S4.F2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/312;" width="476" height="312" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 2: </span>Complete system architecture showing data flow between BO-LLM components.</figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="alg2" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 2</span> </span> Expand function</figcaption>
<div id="alg2.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg2.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            <math id="alg2.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sp</annotation></semantics></math>: seed prompt; <math id="alg2.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>: evaluation batch

</div>
<div id="alg2.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            Evaluate prompt <math id="alg2.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>p</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="alg2.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and collect errors:
<math id="alg2.l2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=\{(x_{i},y_{i}):(x_{i},y_{i})\in B_{\alpha}\wedge LLM_{p}(x_{i})\neq y_{i}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo rspace="0.278em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>∧</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>p</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=\{(x_{i},y_{i}):(x_{i},y_{i})\in B_{\alpha}\wedge LLM_{p}(x_{i})\neq y_{i}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
            Get gradient-inspired edits: <math id="alg2.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{g_{1},...,g_{m}\}=LLM_{\nabla}(sp,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>∇</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{g_{1},...,g_{m}\}=LLM_{\nabla}(sp,e)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
            Use edits to create new prompts:
<math id="alg2.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{\prime}_{i1},...,p^{\prime}_{iq}\}=LLM_{\delta}(p,g_{i},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{\prime}_{i1},...,p^{\prime}_{iq}\}=LLM_{\delta}(p,g_{i},e)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
            Get Monte Carlo successors for diversity:
<math id="alg2.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{\prime\prime}_{ij1},...,p^{\prime\prime}_{ijm}\}=LLM_{mc}(p^{\prime}_{ij})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{\prime\prime}_{ij1},...,p^{\prime\prime}_{ijm}\}=LLM_{mc}(p^{\prime}_{ij})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg2.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
            Remove seed prompt <math id="alg2.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sp</annotation></semantics></math> to avoid re-testing

</div>
<div id="alg2.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg2.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg2.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg2.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{\prime}_{11},...,p^{\prime}_{mq}\}\cup\{p^{\prime\prime}_{111},...,p^{\prime\prime}_{mqp}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>11</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>111</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{\prime}_{11},...,p^{\prime}_{mq}\}\cup\{p^{\prime\prime}_{111},...,p^{\prime\prime}_{mqp}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">IV-B</span> </span><span id="S4.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prompt Generation via Expansion</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The optimization loop generates new candidate prompts from high-performing seeds. The expansion process, outlined in Algorithm <a href="#alg2" title="Algorithm 2 ‣ IV-A System Architecture ‣ IV Implementation of BO-LLM ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>, uses an LLM to generate edits inspired by classification errors on minibatch <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, combined with Monte Carlo rewrites for diversity.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Algorithm <a href="#alg3" title="Algorithm 3 ‣ IV-B Prompt Generation via Expansion ‣ IV Implementation of BO-LLM ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> integrates the expansion mechanism
with the GP surrogate and UCB acquisition. Starting from the top-3
seeds in the cache, it generates candidates via the expand function,
evaluates each on the control minibatch <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> to obtain prediction vectors <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{p}</annotation></semantics></math>, and uses the GP posterior to compute acquisition scores. The candidate maximizing UCB is selected for evaluation on <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="alg3" class="ltx_float ltx_float_algorithm ltx_framed ltx_framed_top">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_float"><span id="alg3.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Algorithm 3</span> </span> Acquisition Optimization (UCB with GP over prediction vectors)</figcaption>
<div id="alg3.3" class="ltx_listing ltx_framed ltx_framed_topbottom ltx_listing">
<div id="alg3.l1" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">1:</span></span>
              
            Posterior GP over prompts via prediction vectors on <math id="alg3.l1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math>;
evaluation batch <math id="alg3.l1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><mo>⊂</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}\subset\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math>; seed pool <math id="alg3.l1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l2" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">2:</span></span>
              
            <math id="alg3.l2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\leftarrow\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\leftarrow\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l2.2" class="ltx_text" style="float:right;"><math id="alg3.l2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\triangleright" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⊳</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\triangleright</annotation></semantics></math> candidate set
</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l3" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">3:</span></span>
              
            Select <math id="alg3.l3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n{=}3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n{=}3</annotation></semantics></math> best seeds by observed accuracy in <math id="alg3.l3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{D}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>D</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{D}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l4" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l4.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">4:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg3.l4.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each seed <math id="alg3.l4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sp</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l4.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l5" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l5.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">5:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg3.l5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e\leftarrow\{(x,y)\!\in\!B_{\alpha}:\ \mathrm{LLM}_{sp}(x)\!\neq\!y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LLM</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.108em" rspace="0.108em">≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e\leftarrow\{(x,y)\!\in\!B_{\alpha}:\ \mathrm{LLM}_{sp}(x)\!\neq\!y\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l6" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l6.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">6:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg3.l6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{g_{i}\}_{i=1}^{4}\leftarrow\mathrm{LLM}_{\nabla}(sp,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>4</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LLM</mi><mo>∇</mo></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{g_{i}\}_{i=1}^{4}\leftarrow\mathrm{LLM}_{\nabla}(sp,e)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l7" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l7.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">7:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg3.l7.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> each <math id="alg3.l7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l7.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l8" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l8.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">8:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg3.l8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}\leftarrow\mathrm{LLM}_{\delta}(sp,g_{i},e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LLM</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}\leftarrow\mathrm{LLM}_{\delta}(sp,g_{i},e)</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l9" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l9.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">9:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg3.l9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{p^{\prime\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{2}\leftarrow\mathrm{LLM}_{mc}(p^{\prime})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>j</mi><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><msub><mi>LLM</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{p^{\prime\prime}_{j}\}_{j=1}^{2}\leftarrow\mathrm{LLM}_{mc}(p^{\prime})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l10" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l10.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">10:</span></span>
              
               <math id="alg3.l10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C\leftarrow C\cup\{p^{\prime},p^{\prime\prime}_{1},p^{\prime\prime}_{2}\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>C</mi><mo>∪</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C\leftarrow C\cup\{p^{\prime},p^{\prime\prime}_{1},p^{\prime\prime}_{2}\}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l11" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l11.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">11:</span></span>
              
              <span id="alg3.l11.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l11.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l12" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l12.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">12:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg3.l12.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l12.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l13" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l13.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">13:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg3.l13.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span> <math id="alg3.l13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p\in C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p\in C</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="alg3.l13.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">do</span>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l14" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l14.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">14:</span></span>
              
              <math id="alg3.l14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{y}_{p}\leftarrow\mathrm{evaluate}(p,B_{GP})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mi>evaluate</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{y}_{p}\leftarrow\mathrm{evaluate}(p,B_{GP})</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l15" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l15.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">15:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg3.l15.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">end</span> <span id="alg3.l15.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">for</span>
</div>
<div id="alg3.l16" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l16.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">16:</span></span>
              
            Compute <math id="alg3.l16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu(p),\sigma(p)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>σ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu(p),\sigma(p)</annotation></semantics></math> from GP on <math id="alg3.l16.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{\hat{y}_{p}\}_{p\in C}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>y</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>p</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{\hat{y}_{p}\}_{p\in C}</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
<div id="alg3.l17" class="ltx_listingline">
              <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_listingline"><span id="alg3.l17.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:80%;">17:</span></span>
              
            <span id="alg3.l17.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">return</span> <math id="alg3.l17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}=\arg\max_{p\in C}\big[\mu(p)+\kappa\,\sigma(p)\big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><msub><mi>max</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi>C</mi></mrow></msub><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>κ</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>σ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>p</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}=\arg\max_{p\in C}\big[\mu(p)+\kappa\,\sigma(p)\big]</annotation></semantics></math>

</div>
</div>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">IV-C</span> </span><span id="S4.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Flowchart</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F3" title="Fig. 3 ‣ IV-C Flowchart ‣ IV Implementation of BO-LLM ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a> summarizes the iterative optimization process of BO-LLM.
The algorithm proceeds in a closed loop where each round consists of: (1) generating candidate prompts via the Expand function, (2) fitting a GP surrogate on cached observations, (3) selecting the highest-scoring candidate via UCB, (4) evaluating the selected prompt on minibatch <math id="S4.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, and (5) updating the cache and seed pool. The backward edge from ”Update cache and seeds” to ”Expand” represents the
iterative refinement process that continues until convergence or a maximum number of rounds is reached.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F3" class="ltx_figure"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F3.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering" height="310.41" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 437.88 310.41" width="437.88"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="translate(0,310.41) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0) translate(179.3,0) translate(0,294.39)"><g stroke-width="0.4pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.48 15.75 L -173.48 15.75 C -176.54 15.75 -179.02 13.27 -179.02 10.21 L -179.02 -10.21 C -179.02 -13.27 -176.54 -15.75 -173.48 -15.75 L 173.48 -15.75 C 176.54 -15.75 179.02 -13.27 179.02 -10.21 L 179.02 10.21 C 179.02 13.27 176.54 15.75 173.48 15.75 Z M -179.02 -15.75"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -41.18 -3.46)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.95em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="82.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Seed prompts</span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.48 -39.92 L -173.48 -39.92 C -176.54 -39.92 -179.02 -42.4 -179.02 -45.46 L -179.02 -65.88 C -179.02 -68.94 -176.54 -71.42 -173.48 -71.42 L 173.48 -71.42 C 176.54 -71.42 179.02 -68.94 179.02 -65.88 L 179.02 -45.46 C 179.02 -42.4 176.54 -39.92 173.48 -39.92 Z M -179.02 -71.42"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -89.38 -59.13)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:12.92em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="178.77"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Expand: edits + MC rewrites</span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.48 -95.6 L -173.48 -95.6 C -176.54 -95.6 -179.02 -98.07 -179.02 -101.13 L -179.02 -121.56 C -179.02 -124.61 -176.54 -127.09 -173.48 -127.09 L 173.48 -127.09 C 176.54 -127.09 179.02 -124.61 179.02 -121.56 L 179.02 -101.13 C 179.02 -98.07 176.54 -95.6 173.48 -95.6 Z M -179.02 -127.09"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -44.3 -114.73)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:3.78em;--ltx-fo-height:0.68em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.46" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.46)" width="52.37"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Fit GP <math id="S4.F3.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Rightarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo stretchy="false">⇒</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Rightarrow</annotation></semantics></math><math id="S4.F3.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu,\sigma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>μ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>σ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu,\sigma</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.48 -151.27 L -173.48 -151.27 C -176.54 -151.27 -179.02 -153.74 -179.02 -156.8 L -179.02 -177.23 C -179.02 -180.28 -176.54 -182.76 -173.48 -182.76 L 173.48 -182.76 C 176.54 -182.76 179.02 -180.28 179.02 -177.23 L 179.02 -156.8 C 179.02 -153.74 176.54 -151.27 173.48 -151.27 Z M -179.02 -182.76"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -80.31 -171.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:11.58em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="160.24"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">UCB select best candidate</span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.48 -206.94 L -173.48 -206.94 C -176.54 -206.94 -179.02 -209.42 -179.02 -212.47 L -179.02 -232.9 C -179.02 -235.96 -176.54 -238.43 -173.48 -238.43 L 173.48 -238.43 C 176.54 -238.43 179.02 -235.96 179.02 -232.9 L 179.02 -212.47 C 179.02 -209.42 176.54 -206.94 173.48 -206.94 Z M -179.02 -238.43"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -47.88 -226.45)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:5.6em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="9.61" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="77.45"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Evaluate on <math id="S4.F3.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></foreignObject></g><path style="fill:none" d="M 173.48 -262.61 L -173.48 -262.61 C -176.54 -262.61 -179.02 -265.09 -179.02 -268.14 L -179.02 -288.57 C -179.02 -291.63 -176.54 -294.11 -173.48 -294.11 L 173.48 -294.11 C 176.54 -294.11 179.02 -291.63 179.02 -288.57 L 179.02 -268.14 C 179.02 -265.09 176.54 -262.61 173.48 -262.61 Z M -179.02 -294.11"></path><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 -72.14 -281.82)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:10.43em;--ltx-fo-height:0.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.19em;font-size:10pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="144.29"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">Update cache and seeds</span></span></foreignObject></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -16.02 L 0 -31.07"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -31.07)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -71.7 L 0 -86.74"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -86.74)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -127.37 L 0 -142.41"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -142.41)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -183.04 L 0 -198.08"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -198.08)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 0 -238.71 L 0 -253.75"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(0.0 -1.0 1.0 0.0 0 -253.75)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g><g stroke-width="0.8pt"><path style="fill:none" d="M 179.29 -278.36 L 258.03 -278.36 L 258.03 -55.67 L 187.87 -55.67"></path><g stroke-dasharray="none" stroke-dashoffset="0.0pt" stroke-linejoin="miter" transform="matrix(-1.0 0.0 0.0 -1.0 187.87 -55.67)"><path d="M 6.37 0 C 5.58 0.19 2.15 1.28 0 2.46 L 0 -2.46 C 2.15 -1.28 5.58 -0.19 6.37 0 Z"></path></g></g></g></svg></span>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 3: </span>BO-LLM optimization loop.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">IV-D</span> </span><span id="S4.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Additional Details</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">During the expansion phase, each seed prompt generates candidates through a cascade of LLM operations with the following parameters:</p>
<ul id="S4.I1" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">4 gradient-inspired edits per seed (via <math id="S4.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LLM_{\nabla}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mo>∇</mo></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LLM_{\nabla}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">1 edit application step per gradient (via <math id="S4.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LLM_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LLM_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">2 Monte Carlo paraphrases per edited prompt (via <math id="S4.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="LLM_{mc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">LLM_{mc}</annotation></semantics></math>)</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Resulting in approximately 3 unique candidates per seed after deduplication</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The prompts are evaluated using a Cached01Scorer that maintains a cache of previously evaluated prompt-accuracy pairs to avoid redundant API calls. The UCB hyperparameter <math id="S4.SS4.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\kappa" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>κ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\kappa</annotation></semantics></math> is annealed linearly from 2.0 to 0.5 over 10 rounds, transitioning from exploration to exploitation.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS4.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS4.p3.1" class="ltx_p">For the expansion function, we generate 4 <math id="S4.SS4.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>g</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g</annotation></semantics></math> gradients, with 1 gradient per error, 1 step per gradient, 2 Monte Carlo samples per stem, and 3 prompt generations per seed prompt. The evaluator is set to UCB and the scorer is set to the Cached01Scorer.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS5.4" class="ltx_text">IV-E</span> </span><span id="S4.SS5.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Comparison with ProTeGi</span></h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ProTeGi proceeds in multiple candidates per round: gradient-inspired edits, beam search, and Monte-Carlo rewrites. It keeps top-<math id="S4.SS5.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> as new seeds, improving stability but with <math id="S4.SS5.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>m</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m</annotation></semantics></math>-fold higher API cost. BO-LLM differs by fitting a surrogate and selecting one candidate per round.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ProTeGi pipeline (gradient, edits, MC).</h4>

<div id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">ProTeGi <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">14</a>]</cite> operates in rounds starting from seed prompts <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sp</annotation></semantics></math> and an eval minibatch <math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> with three LLM roles:</p>
<ul id="S4.I2" class="ltx_itemize ltx_leftmargin_flush">
<li id="S4.I2.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{LLM}_{\nabla}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐋𝐋𝐌</mi><mo>∇</mo></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{LLM}_{\nabla}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em id="S4.I2.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">gradient-inspired edits</em>): consume <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(sp,e)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi>e</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(sp,e)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e=\{(x,y)\in B_{\alpha}:\ \mathrm{LLM}_{sp}(x)\neq y\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.778em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>LLM</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≠</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e=\{(x,y)\in B_{\alpha}:\ \mathrm{LLM}_{sp}(x)\neq y\}</annotation></semantics></math> and propose textual “gradients” <math id="S4.I2.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{1},\dots,g_{m}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{1},\dots,g_{m}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{LLM}_{\delta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐋𝐋𝐌</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{LLM}_{\delta}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em id="S4.I2.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">edit applier</em>): apply <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="sp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">sp</annotation></semantics></math> to form candidates <math id="S4.I2.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{i1},\dots,p^{\prime}_{iq}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{i1},\dots,p^{\prime}_{iq}</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S4.I2.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S4.I2.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><math id="S4.I2.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbf{LLM}_{mc}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>𝐋𝐋𝐌</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbf{LLM}_{mc}</annotation></semantics></math> (<em id="S4.I2.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Monte-Carlo rewrites</em>): paraphrase <math id="S4.I2.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime}_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime}_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> to explore local neighborhoods, producing <math id="S4.I2.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{\prime\prime}_{ij1},\dots,p^{\prime\prime}_{ijr}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mo>′′</mo></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{\prime\prime}_{ij1},\dots,p^{\prime\prime}_{ijr}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Candidates are scored on a minibatch; a beam/top-<math id="S4.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> policy keeps several high scorers as next-round seeds. This multi-candidate policy improves stability at the cost of higher API usage. BO-LLM instead fits a surrogate on prediction patterns and typically selects a single most-informative candidate via UCB.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S4.SS6.4" class="ltx_text">IV-F</span> </span><span id="S4.SS6.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Practical Considerations</span></h3>

<section id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Evaluation noise.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Even with identical prompts, we observed 5–10% variation in accuracy due to LLM nondeterminism. To mitigate this, BO-LLM applies a variance floor <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sigma_{\min}=0.02" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>min</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.02</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sigma_{\min}=0.02</annotation></semantics></math> and allows repeated evaluation when the UCB margin is small.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Label-reversal pitfalls.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Occasionally a candidate prompt implicitly reverses labels (e.g., mapping “true” to 0 and “false” to 1). Such prompts may achieve misleading minibatch accuracy and contaminate the seed pool. We detect these cases by checking confusion patterns against a reference prompt.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Stability vs. cost.</h4>

<div id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Selecting only one candidate per round yields <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(T)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>T</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(T)</annotation></semantics></math> API calls, but is more prone to local maxima. Batch-UCB with <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="m=3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">m=3</annotation></semantics></math> improves stability but requires <math id="S4.SS6.SSS0.Px3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\approx 3\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0.222em">×</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\approx 3\times</annotation></semantics></math> calls.
This trade-off is analyzed further in our ablation studies.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">V </span><span id="S5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Experiments</span></h2>

<section id="S5.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS1.4" class="ltx_text">V-A</span> </span><span id="S5.SS1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Setup and Datasets</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We compare BO-LLM with ProTeGi on LIAR <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">12</a>]</cite> and ETHOS <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">13</a>]</cite>. The LIAR dataset contains 12.8k political statements labeled for truthfulness, which we map to a binary task (true vs. false). The ETHOS dataset contains over 8k social media comments labeled for hate speech (hate vs. non-hate).</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">Each algorithm is run for 10 rounds, starting with the same initial prompt for fair comparison. For BO-LLM, the control minibatch <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> has 75 items, and the evaluation minibatch <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> has 50 items. To mitigate potential biases from class imbalance, the control minibatch <math id="S5.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> was sampled to maintain the original dataset’s label distribution. Accuracy is reported on held-out test sets, averaged over three runs.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS2.4" class="ltx_text">V-B</span> </span><span id="S5.SS2.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Evaluation Protocol</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We report test accuracy from three independent runs with different
random seeds. Both BO-LLM and ProTeGi start from the same initial
seed prompt for fair comparison. Each algorithm runs for <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=10</annotation></semantics></math>
rounds with identical API budgets. For BO-LLM, the control minibatch
<math id="S5.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{GP}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>P</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{GP}</annotation></semantics></math> contains 75 items, and the evaluation minibatch <math id="S5.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B_{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>α</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B_{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>
contains 50 items.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each run, we record the best accuracy achieved across all rounds. The reported results show the trajectory of the best prompt found up to each round, averaged across the three runs. We also report the standard deviation to capture the variance in LLM evaluations, which ranges from 5–10% even for identical prompts due to model nondeterminism <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite">[<a href="#bib.bib22" title="" class="ltx_ref">22</a>]</cite>.
This protocol ensures a fair and statistically robust comparison between methods.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS3.4" class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span id="S5.SS3.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Results</span></h3>

<figure id="S5.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.04384v1/liar_figure.png" id="S5.F4.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/161;" width="215" height="161" alt="Refer to caption"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2"><img src="2510.04384v1/ethos_figure.png" id="S5.F4.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:215/161;" width="215" height="161" alt="Refer to caption"></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Fig. 4: </span>Comparison of BO-LLM and ProTeGi on LIAR and ETHOS datasets over 10 rounds.</figcaption>
</figure>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">LIAR Dataset</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On the LIAR dataset, both algorithms show similar upward trends in accuracy over 10 rounds. ProTeGi reached a peak accuracy of <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">60.0%</span> at round 9, while BO-LLM peaked at <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">58.5%</span> at round 7. Compared to the initial prompt’s performance, BO-LLM achieved a 32% relative improvement versus 27.7% for ProTeGi. The variance across rounds remains high for both, reflecting the ambiguous nature of political statements.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ETHOS Dataset</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On the ETHOS dataset, BO-LLM slightly outperformed ProTeGi, achieving a peak accuracy of <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">95.75%</span> at round 7 compared to ProTeGi’s <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">94.5%</span> at round 2. The relative accuracy gains over the initial prompt were <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">8.2%</span> for BO-LLM and <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">7.4%</span> for ProTeGi. BO-LLM also appeared to converge more quickly, with accuracy stabilizing by round 5.</p>
</div>
<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">It must be noted that the initial prompt for the BO-LLM and ProTeGi algorithms are the same. The variability in LLM accuracy with the same prompt on the LIAR dataset can be seen on the 0th round as the two algorithms began with the same prompt yet the LLM obtained slightly different accuracies for it. This will therefore influence the relative accuracy increase both algorithms were able to achieve.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection"><span id="S5.SS4.4" class="ltx_text">V-D</span> </span><span id="S5.SS4.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Prompt Evolution Analysis</span></h3>

<div id="S5.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S5.T1" title="TABLE I ‣ V-D Prompt Evolution Analysis ‣ V Experiments ‣ LLM Based Bayesian Optimization for Prompt Search" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a> shows how BO-LLM iteratively refines prompts on the LIAR dataset, incorporating task-relevant features that progressively improve accuracy.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S5.T1" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">TABLE I: </span>Prompt evolution on LIAR dataset</figcaption>
<table id="S5.T1.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S5.T1.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S5.T1.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S5.T1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:22.8pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.1.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Iter.</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt">
<span id="S5.T1.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Prompt</span></span>
</span></th>
<th id="S5.T1.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S5.T1.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;">Acc.</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S5.T1.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.2.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:22.8pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.2.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.2.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.2.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Determine whether the Statement is a lie (Yes) or not (No) based on the Context and other information.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.470</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:22.8pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.3.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.3.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">1</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.3.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.3.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.3.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Determine whether the Statement is a lie (Yes) or not (No) based on the Context, the individual’s Job title, State, and Party affiliation.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.1.3.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.535</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.1.4" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.1.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.4.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:22.8pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.4.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.4.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">3</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Determine whether the Statement is a lie (Yes) or not (No) based on the source’s job title, state, party affiliation, and context. Consider the credibility and bias of the source.</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_nopad_r ltx_align_center ltx_border_t"><span id="S5.T1.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">0.540</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S5.T1.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S5.T1.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.5.1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:22.8pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.5.1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.5.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">5</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S5.T1.1.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top ltx_border_bb ltx_border_t">
<span id="S5.T1.1.5.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:170.7pt;">
<span id="S5.T1.1.5.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.T1.1.5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Decide if the Statement is false (Yes) or true (No) by considering the credibility and bias of the source, along with the content and factual accuracy.</span></span>
</span></td>
